NAME
    rsudo-admin - interactive rsudo administration console

SYNOPSIS
    rsudo-admin

DESCRIPTION
    rsudo-admin is an m-owned terminal console that composes the existing rsudo,
    menu, editor, vsed and encrypted-file facilities into recurring
    administrative workflows.

    The main menu contains:

        Connect to host
        Browse host
        rsudo jobs
        Encrypted file load/edit/new

    The command accepts no operands or options. Escape from the main menu exits
    successfully.

HOST DISCOVERY
    Connect to host and Browse host discover credential groups already present
    in the current rsudo-admin shell by matching shell variables named:

        RSUDO_CREDENTIALS_GROUP_<group>_HOST

    <group> must be a valid shell identifier and the HOST value must be
    non-empty. The menu displays the host plus its group identity. Selecting an
    entry selects the corresponding credential group through current rsudo
    --load :group semantics.

    Credential groups normally become available by using the encrypted-file
    Load action during the same rsudo-admin session, or from state already
    present when rsudo-admin starts.

CONNECT TO HOST
    Connect to host opens the host selector and, after selection, starts:

        rsudo --load :group --interactive

    The operation runs in an action-local subshell. rsudo reusable mode state
    selected by the interactive session therefore does not leak into later
    rsudo-admin actions.

BROWSE HOST
    Browse host opens the host selector and injects the existing m filesystem
    menu into the selected privileged remote rsudo session.

    The injected dependency set is explicitly:

        base
        array
        map
        term
        menu

    The injected one-shot command is the current local bin/sys/menu source with:

        -d /

    Remote menu standard output is discarded by rsudo-admin; the terminal UI is
    the browsing interface. The action runs in a subshell so its rsudo mode
    state does not alter the surrounding console session.

RSUDO JOBS
    rsudo jobs modernizes the former tracked rsudo-jobs-template workflow using
    current m facilities.

    The workflow is:

        1. select one readable local shell library source with the file browser;
        2. select one readable local shell template with the file browser;
        3. source the selected library inside a job subshell;
        4. copy the template to a private temporary file;
        5. edit the temporary copy through editor;
        6. validate the edited copy with POSIX sh -n;
        7. execute the edited copy as shell source in a nested subshell;
        8. remove the temporary copy on every normal or trapped job exit.

    File selection starts in the rsudo-admin invocation directory and may browse
    elsewhere. The selected library and template are explicit executable shell
    code. Sourcing them is the purpose of this workflow, not data parsing.

    The job subshell inherits credential groups and other shell state available
    to rsudo-admin. Job-local definitions, exit, traps and other process-local
    effects do not persist back into the main console. The temporary edited copy
    is created under ${TMPDIR:-/tmp} with private creation permissions.

ENCRYPTED FILE LOAD/EDIT/NEW
    This entry opens one filesystem browser with these action keys:

        l   load
        e   edit
        n   new

    Enter browses directories and Escape returns to the main menu.

    Load
        Requires a readable regular file and calls:

            encoded_file_eval file

        Therefore Load follows the current enc.lib.sh contract: the file is
        completely authenticated/decrypted before evaluation, then its plaintext
        is evaluated as POSIX shell source in the current rsudo-admin shell.
        Variables and functions established by the encrypted source can remain
        available to later menu actions.

    Edit
        Requires a readable/writable regular file and calls:

            encoded_file_edit file

        Editing uses vsed's memory-only plaintext editor path and commits only
        encrypted output according to enc.lib.sh.

    New
        Creates a new encrypted file in the selected directory, or in the
        containing directory when the selected browser item is not a directory.
        rsudo-admin prompts for the new leaf name, opens an empty document in
        vsed, holds the saved plaintext only in process memory, encrypts it to a
        private sibling temporary ciphertext file, and publishes the new file
        only after encryption succeeds.

        New refuses an empty name, '.', '..', a name containing '/', or an
        already existing destination. Cancellation leaves no destination file.

SECURITY
    Credential passwords are not included in host menu labels.

    Host discovery does not export credential state. It inspects current shell
    state and exposes only matching group identities and HOST labels to menu.

    Browse host does not eval the remote menu result locally.

    rsudo jobs intentionally sources user-selected local shell code. Use only
    trusted job libraries and templates.

    Encrypted-file Load intentionally follows encoded_file_eval's authenticated
    shell-source evaluation contract.

    New encrypted files do not use plaintext temporary files. Portable POSIX
    shell cannot guarantee memory zeroization or protection from operating-system
    paging, process inspection, terminal capture or equivalent host mechanisms.

EXIT STATUS
    0   main menu exited normally
    1   invalid command invocation
    2   unrecoverable local menu/runtime setup failure

    Failures of an individual connection, remote browser, job, encrypted load,
    encrypted edit or encrypted creation are reported in the console and return
    control to the main menu instead of terminating the console.

    Signal-derived statuses from interrupted underlying interactive operations
    may be propagated when the console itself cannot continue normally.

